,"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000095464","entrez_id":["5146"],"uniprot":["P51160"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes the alpha-prime subunit of cone phosphodiesterase, which is composed of a homodimer of two alpha-prime subunits and 3 smaller proteins of 11, 13, and 15 kDa. Mutations in this gene are associated with cone dystrophy type 4 (COD4). [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P51160","text":"Catalytic alpha subunit of the cone-specific cGMP phosphodiesterase (PDE6) complex, which hydrolyzes 3',5'-cyclic GMP as part of the phototransduction cascade. The PDE6 holoenzyme consists of two catalytic alpha subunits (PDE6C) and two inhibitory gamma subunits (PDE6H) (PubMed:21127010, PubMed:28583373, PubMed:39739818). Light-activated GNAT2 relieves gamma subunit-mediated inhibition, allowing the catalytic subunits to hydrolyze cGMP and mediate visual signal transduction and amplification. The resulting decrease in cytosolic cGMP levels triggers the closure of cGMP-gated cation channels at the plasma membrane, leading to hyperpolarization of cone photoreceptors (By similarity). The catalytic site can adopt partially open conformations even in the inhibited state, contributing to the higher basal activity and rapid response kinetics characteristic of cones compared to rods (PubMed:39739818)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}